  "body": "**Scoped negative result, no new \u03ba.** In the abelian bit model of #468, two invertible rational 3\u00d73 data targets still need six rank-one calls with one or two *clean* auxiliary registers (zero on input, restored to zero). Six suffice. Merged #1882 settled *dirty* auxiliaries for any register count and explicitly excluded clean ones. Clean correctness is strictly weaker: only the data columns of the endpoint are constrained.\n\n## What is new\n\n- **Clean low-span lemma.** #468 \u00a73 / #1882 Lemma 2 survive clean ancillas. The projected rank argument reads only the data columns of `P\u2212I`, so the auxiliary columns may be arbitrary. At five calls, the relation lattice therefore has rank \u2264 1.\n- **Exhaustive check with the #1882 engine.** The acceptance predicate is relaxed to data columns; nothing else changes.\n\n| Run | Words | Clean terminals | Clean-only | Candidates |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| `n=3`, five calls (one clean ancilla) | 17,210,368 | 4,051,444 | 4,014,687 | **0** |\n| `n=4`, five calls (two clean ancillas) | 24,883,200,000 | 4,012,291,456 | 4,012,108,024 | **0** |\n\n\"Clean-only\" counts terminals that fail #1882's dirty predicate. Almost every surviving terminal uses the relaxation, and none gives two rank-three targets.\n\n## Controls\n\n- **Regression:** dirty mode reproduces #1882's pinned `n=3, s=5` terminal digest byte for byte.\n- **Positive:** one target in three calls gives 64 candidates. Six calls with one clean ancilla gives 310,528.\n- **Failure:** the out-of-model rank-two idempotent `E\u2080\u2080+E\u2081\u2081` gives 134,082 false savings at five calls.\n- **Physical realisation:** 300 clean and 300 clean-only `n=3` terminals, plus 300 clean-only `n=4` terminals, are rebuilt with exact rational frames having exactly the stated relation lattice. Each formal product satisfies the clean predicate, and the clean-only ones fail the dirty predicate.\n- **Independent symbolic check:** agrees with the engine on all `n=2` words, all 614,656 `n=3, s=4` words (full mode), and 3,646 `n=3, s=5` words.\n- **Clean-only identity:** an explicit two-call word that is correct only because the ancilla is zero is accepted, and its leaking variant is rejected.\n- **Tamper controls:** a dropped terminal, an altered representative, a false flag and a wrong-arity record are all rejected.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n```sh\npython3 -B research/bit-clean-ancilla-registers/verify.py          # ~1 min\npython3 -B research/bit-clean-ancilla-registers/verify.py --full   # ~2.7 hours, adds n=4 and s=6\n```\n\nExpected: `PASS_CLEAN_ANCILLA_SIX_CALLS`. Terminal streams are hashed rather than stored, because the full runs emit tens of GB. `RESULT.json` is the recorded full replay (macOS arm64, Python 3.11.9, Apple clang). A separate standalone `n=4` run gave the same digest. `scripts/research_package.py --check-only` passes.\n\n## Scope / not covered\n\n- Covers one and two clean ancillas. **Any number of clean ancillas is open**, because #1882's written Lemma 1 reads auxiliary columns.\n- Three data registers with a clean ancilla at eight calls is not attempted.\n- #288 \u00a71.3(b) already charges clean ancillas, so this closes a route; it does not remove a charge.\n- No change to \u03ba, the selected record, `upstream/` or frozen evidence. Not a Lean proof.\n\nTask: `bit-new-register-model` (scope key `7084092dd726e7ba1f2f`), scope refined (auxiliary input convention), research base `e112d71c`, rebased onto current main `0fdd7d82` (quick replay re-passed before rebase; package-only diff). The helper's random draw was `adversarial-audit`. I switched cards because this question continues directly from my merged #1882, and the overlap check found no prior work on clean ancillas in this model; #1882 and #1822 explicitly exclude them. Claim: #2073. Overlap was checked at start and again before submission.\n\nCredit: Ali Romman (#468: model and low-span lemma), eumemic (#288: model and ancilla pricing), huxint (#203). The engine and controls are adapted from #1882. Prepared by waynenilsen with substantial assistance from Claude (Anthropic). No independent human review is claimed.\n\nFeedback: the generated `VERIFY.json` caps commands at 600 s, so the ~2 h exhaustive run can only be registered as `--full` outside the launcher.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
